      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 45 year old female had grouped pruritic Papules and vesicles with a few scattered tensebullae, symetrically distributed on the extensor surfaces of limbs, back and buttocks. Nikolsky's sign' was negative. Histopathology revealed intra-epidermal suprabasal cleft along with acantholysis. Eosinophilic spongiosis was also present. The patient recovered with dapsone."},
